.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B fifo_ipc.sh
library provides an autonomous, zero-daemon, POSIX-compliant agentic SDK implemented strictly in Bash and GAWK.
It enables concurrent processes, subagents, and tools to communicate reliably without requiring an external broker (such as Redis or RabbitMQ) or Rust sidecar daemons.
.PP
All state transitions, locking mechanisms, and buffering primitives adhere to strict POSIX filesystem semantics.

.SH ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANTS
.TP
.B 1. Kernel Write Atomicity (PIPE_BUF)
POSIX guarantees that any write of \fBPIPE_BUF\fR bytes (4096 bytes on Linux) or fewer to a FIFO is atomic and will not be interleaved with writes from other processes.
\fBipc_send\fR strictly enforces this constraint. Payloads exceeding 3800 bytes are saved to an immutable spillover file in \fI$FIFO_IPC_DIR/payloads/<uuid>.payload\fR, and the frame carries a \fB__spillover_ref__\fR reference which \fBipc_recv\fR transparently resolves.
.TP
.B 2. Sliding Window Credit Flow Control
To prevent producers from overflowing kernel pipe buffers (which causes blocking or broken pipes), channels initialize with a discrete credit window (default 5).
Producers must call \fBipc_flow_acquire\fR (or use \fBipc_send\fR) which consumes one credit token from \fIstate.json\fR under atomic lock.
Consumers call \fBipc_flow_grant\fR (or rely on \fBipc_recv\fR's \fIauto_grant\fR) to replenish credit tokens and signal producers via \fIctrl.fifo\fR.
.TP
.B 3. Backpressure Signaling
Consumers can assert immediate backpressure via \fBipc_flow_pause\fR, setting the \fBbackpressure\fR boolean in channel state.
Waiting writers will hold execution until \fBipc_flow_resume\fR is signaled.
.TP
.B 4. Correlation & Multiplexing
Frames are tagged with monotonic sequence counters (\fBseq\fR), message types (\fBtype\fR), and unique correlation identifiers (\fBuuid\fR).
\fBipc_recv\fR allows selective message ingestion filtered by type or UUID, enabling deterministic request-response handshakes across shared channels.
.TP
.B 5. Promise Pipelining (Monadic Chains)
\fBipc_pipe\fR enables functional composition of async tasks.
When promise A resolves, its output is substituted into the command template for promise B and executed without blocking the orchestrating process.
.TP
.B 6. Process Tree Cleanup on Timeout
Unlike conventional shell background execution, \fBipc_await\fR terminates the entire process group (\fBpkill -P\fR) upon timeout (exit code 124), preventing runaway orphan processes.

.SH RETURN VALUES & ERROR CODES
All functions return standard integers aligned with UNIX errno conventions:
.TP
.B 0 (IPC_OK)
Success.
.TP
.B 1 (IPC_ERR_GENERIC)
Internal generic error.
.TP
.B 2 (IPC_ERR_NOTFOUND)
Channel, promise, or file not found (ENOENT).
.TP
.B 13 (IPC_ERR_PERMISSION)
Permission denied or lock inaccessible (EACCES).
.TP
.B 16 (IPC_ERR_BUSY)
Channel state locked by another process (EBUSY).
.TP
.B 22 (IPC_ERR_INVALID)
Invalid argument or malformed JSON frame (EINVAL).
.TP
.B 32 (IPC_ERR_PIPE)
Broken FIFO pipe or channel aborted by peer (EPIPE).
.TP
.B 110 (IPC_ERR_TIMEOUT)
Credit acquisition or flow control timed out (ETIMEDOUT).
.TP
.B 124 (IPC_ERR_AWAIT_TIMEOUT)
Promise await barrier timed out; worker killed.
.TP
.B 125 (IPC_ERR_CANCELED)
Task was explicitly canceled.
.TP
.B 137 (IPC_ERR_CRASH)
Worker process terminated abnormally or killed by SIGKILL.

.SH CODE EXAMPLES
.SS Simple Asynchronous Execution
.PP
.nf
.RS
source "$LODGE_DIR/lib/ipc/fifo_ipc.sh"
ipc_channel_open "subagent-1" 5

# Launch long-running task in background
prom=$(ipc_async "subagent-1" "python3 worker.py --batch-size 32")

# Await completion with 60 second timeout
if output=$(ipc_await "$prom" 60); then
    echo "Task resolved successfully: $output"
else
    echo "Task failed or timed out with exit code $?"
fi

ipc_channel_close "subagent-1"
.RE
.fi

.SS Synchronous Streaming with Flow Control
.PP
.nf
.RS
source "$LODGE_DIR/lib/ipc/fifo_ipc.sh"
ipc_channel_open "stream-1" 3

# Send frame
ipc_send "stream-1" "COMMAND" '{"action":"compute","matrix":"A"}'

# Receive frame with correlation filter
frame=$(ipc_recv "stream-1" 5 "COMMAND")
echo "Received frame: $frame"

ipc_channel_close "stream-1"
.RE
.fi

